WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.531
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:03.801 --> 00:07.508
It reminds me of my time at boot camp, too.

3
00:07.508 --> 00:09.516
When I first went there,

4
00:09.516 --> 00:12.180
everything was new, and everyone was picking a fight,

5
00:12.180 --> 00:13.680
I was so scared.

6
00:13.680 --> 00:14.964
You know, Yeom Il Hwan?

7
00:14.964 --> 00:17.359
He looks scarier than Sergeant Kang Chan Seok.

8
00:17.359 --> 00:18.360
Does he?

9
00:18.360 --> 00:21.191
Yeah, I'm not joking.

10
00:22.162 --> 00:28.153
Anyway, back then, Hyeon Uk was really nice to me.

11
00:28.153 --> 00:32.323
[95th division training camp, a year ago]

12
00:57.232 --> 00:59.434
[Yeom Il Hwan]

13
01:00.392 --> 01:03.799
- Why? - Huh? It's nothing.

14
01:12.922 --> 01:14.422
Hi.

15
01:14.422 --> 01:16.452
Oh, hi!

16
01:16.452 --> 01:17.968
Let's get along!

17
01:17.968 --> 01:20.469
Yeah! Me too!

18
01:20.469 --> 01:23.394
Is your name... Park Min Sik?

19
01:23.394 --> 01:24.395
Oh.

20
01:24.395 --> 01:26.503
No, it's Seok! Park Min Seok!

21
01:26.503 --> 01:28.130
Oh, Min Seok.

22
01:28.130 --> 01:29.441
Yeah.

23
01:29.441 --> 01:31.769
I'm Kim Hyeon Uk.

24
01:31.769 --> 01:32.942
Kim Hyeon Uk.

25
01:32.942 --> 01:34.188
Good to meet you.

26
01:34.188 --> 01:36.668
Good to meet you, too. Let's be nice to each other for the next five weeks.

27
01:36.668 --> 01:38.618
Yeah, me too.

28
01:40.309 --> 01:43.796
You know, drill instructors scared me.

29
01:43.796 --> 01:46.000
When I first got here, they were so nice.

30
01:46.000 --> 01:48.098
But once we got in here, they changed completely.

31
01:48.098 --> 01:49.650
You there.

32
01:49.650 --> 01:51.209
Shut up.

33
01:51.209 --> 01:54.159
- Okay? - Sorry.

34
01:56.037 --> 01:58.472
Did you see the drill instructor's washbasin earlier?

35
01:58.472 --> 01:59.951
That was brutal.

36
01:59.951 --> 02:01.952
I know. It's driving me nuts.

37
02:01.952 --> 02:03.778
You.

38
02:03.778 --> 02:08.241
Shut your mouth before I rip your tongue out, you hicks.

39
02:08.241 --> 02:09.504
You hear me?

40
02:09.504 --> 02:11.063
Do you?

41
02:11.063 --> 02:13.823
- Huh? - You keep quiet.

42
02:15.015 --> 02:17.378
Who the fuck is this now?

43
02:17.378 --> 02:18.519
Do you want a go?

44
02:18.519 --> 02:19.592
- Do you? - Go ahead.

45
02:19.592 --> 02:21.516
- Shouldn't we stop them? - Just leave it.

46
02:21.516 --> 02:23.592
Go ahead, fucker.

47
02:23.592 --> 02:25.196
- Do you or not? - Bring it on.

48
02:25.196 --> 02:26.854
Hey, there.

49
02:26.854 --> 02:28.120
Hey.

50
02:28.120 --> 02:29.758
Keep quiet.

51
02:34.992 --> 02:37.667
[Kwon Tae Woong]

52
02:39.819 --> 02:41.468
Trainees.

53
02:43.183 --> 02:45.444
I don't want to hear your voices outside. Understood?

54
02:45.444 --> 02:47.604
- Understood! - Understood!

55
02:48.313 --> 02:50.224
The time is 17:27.

56
02:50.224 --> 02:52.854
I'll inspect your belongings in ten minutes.

57
02:52.854 --> 02:56.179
Anything you brought from outside is not allowed. Got it?

58
02:56.179 --> 02:57.906
- Understood! - Understood!

59
02:57.906 --> 02:59.832
I can't hear you. Got it?

60
02:59.832 --> 03:01.954
- Understood! - Understood!

61
03:01.954 --> 03:04.722
Glasses and glasses cases are allowed.

62
03:04.722 --> 03:09.517
Check if you've brought something unnecessary and you're still keeping it, especially,

63
03:09.517 --> 03:12.011
if you've sneaked cigarettes and phones, this is your last chance.

64
03:12.011 --> 03:14.247
There won't be a next time.

65
03:14.247 --> 03:15.846
Understood?

66
03:17.279 --> 03:18.819
Understood?

67
03:18.819 --> 03:21.047
- Understood! - Understood!

68
03:29.921 --> 03:30.934
Let's get ready quickly.

69
03:30.934 --> 03:32.267
Yeah.

70
03:41.795 --> 03:44.243
When your packets arrive at your home,

71
03:44.243 --> 03:48.122
[Episode 04: Trainee Kim Hyeon Uk] your parents will shed tears,

72
03:48.122 --> 03:51.266
worrying whether you are doing fine and adapting well.

73
03:51.266 --> 03:52.479
Then what will you tell them?

74
03:52.479 --> 03:54.129
- We tell them we're doing great! - We tell them we're doing great!

75
03:54.129 --> 03:55.573
You should write,

76
03:55.573 --> 03:58.354
"Your brave son will become a soldier defending the country," right?

77
03:58.354 --> 03:59.986
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir.

78
03:59.986 --> 04:03.509
I know some of you will write down song lyrics just because you don't know what to write.

79
04:03.509 --> 04:06.387
Don't be unfilial. Behave, understood?

80
04:06.387 --> 04:08.777
- Understood! - Understood, sir!

81
04:21.875 --> 04:23.825
Trainee 4.

82
04:24.410 --> 04:26.914
You don't have anything to tell your parents?

83
04:27.635 --> 04:28.963
I don't.

84
04:28.963 --> 04:30.297
Are you sure?

85
04:30.297 --> 04:31.298
I am sure.

86
04:31.298 --> 04:36.567
Is it really that hard to write to your parents who raised you and tell them you're doing well?

87
04:36.567 --> 04:38.187
Are you really that ungrateful?

88
04:38.933 --> 04:40.327
I am.

89
04:46.719 --> 04:47.897
Min Seok.

90
04:47.897 --> 04:49.458
Finish writing.

91
04:58.842 --> 05:01.018
Dear my beloved parents,

92
05:01.018 --> 05:03.367
Mom, Dad, are you well?

93
05:03.367 --> 05:05.811
This is your only son, Min Seok.

94
05:05.811 --> 05:07.662
After saying goodbye to you earlier today,

95
05:07.662 --> 05:11.267
I just packed away the clothes and shoes I wore as a civilian.

96
05:11.267 --> 05:14.402
It really hit me that I'm here in the army.

97
05:14.402 --> 05:15.884
When you receive my clothes,

98
05:15.884 --> 05:18.061
please don't cry.

99
05:18.676 --> 05:24.207
I met a very nice guy who will be my battle buddy.

100
05:24.876 --> 05:28.176
Tomorrow, I'll start my drills wearing a combat uniform.

101
05:28.176 --> 05:31.306
I'll stay safe and become a true soldier.

102
05:31.929 --> 05:34.879
So please, don't worry about me.

103
05:35.760 --> 05:37.625
Mom, Dad,

104
05:37.625 --> 05:39.575
I love you.

105
05:46.586 --> 05:48.273
Everything's unfamiliar.

106
05:48.273 --> 05:51.688
The place, the people, and the situation.

107
05:52.792 --> 05:54.549
21 months ahead of me.

108
05:54.549 --> 05:56.699
Can I really do this?

109
05:58.635 --> 06:01.604
No, you got this, Park Min Seok.

110
06:01.604 --> 06:04.691
I'm going to be reborn after this.

111
06:04.691 --> 06:09.563
I'll do my best to become a better man...

112
06:52.287 --> 06:54.591
Straighten your slippers.

113
07:04.861 --> 07:07.608
Now, I'll teach you how to state your rank and name. Understood?

114
07:07.608 --> 07:08.609
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

115
07:08.609 --> 07:10.472
- Louder! Understood? - Yes, sir!

116
07:10.472 --> 07:14.193
In the military, when a superior calls you, you state your rank and name. What do you say?

117
07:14.193 --> 07:15.539
- Rank and name, sir! - Rank and name, sir!

118
07:15.539 --> 07:17.394
Rank and name. What do you say?

119
07:17.394 --> 07:18.934
- Rank and name, sir! - Rank and name, sir!

120
07:18.934 --> 07:19.935
Hey.

121
07:19.935 --> 07:20.956
Yes, sir?

122
07:20.956 --> 07:23.936
Answer like that again, and you'll be shot on the spot. Got it?

123
07:23.936 --> 07:24.937
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

124
07:24.937 --> 07:27.111
I can't hear you! Do you want to get smoked first? Got it?

125
07:27.111 --> 07:28.112
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

126
07:28.112 --> 07:30.973
Since you're still trainees without a rank,

127
07:30.973 --> 07:32.725
you state your number instead of your rank. Got it?

128
07:32.725 --> 07:33.726
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

129
07:33.726 --> 07:36.007
And you'll leave out "sir" at the end. Got it?

130
07:36.007 --> 07:37.418
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

131
07:37.418 --> 07:38.812
Hey.

132
07:39.605 --> 07:40.727
Yes... Oh.

133
07:40.727 --> 07:41.906
T-Trainee 12.

134
07:41.906 --> 07:44.827
- Everyone, get in push-up position. - Push-up position!

135
07:44.827 --> 07:47.062
Did I explain this two days ago?

136
07:47.062 --> 07:48.063
- No, sir! - No, sir!

137
07:48.063 --> 07:50.175
- I told you ten seconds ago. Am I right? - Yes, sir!

138
07:50.175 --> 07:52.375
- Do you have the memory of a goldfish? - No, sir!

139
07:52.375 --> 07:54.135
I'm going to give you another chance. Understood?

140
07:54.135 --> 07:55.136
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

141
07:55.136 --> 07:57.103
- Up. - Up!

142
07:57.859 --> 08:01.778
- Hey. - Trainee 12, Park Min Seok, sir.

143
08:01.778 --> 08:04.866
You'll leave out "sir" at the end. Got it?

144
08:06.403 --> 08:08.046
Who was that?

145
08:14.784 --> 08:17.552
Who the hell just sighed?

146
08:19.836 --> 08:20.837
Are you going to keep quiet?

147
08:20.837 --> 08:23.627
Trainee 4, Yeom Il Hwan, sir.

148
08:24.444 --> 08:25.592
Everyone, down.

149
08:25.592 --> 08:27.569
- Push-up position! - Push-up position!

150
08:28.951 --> 08:31.148
You don't deserve to learn.

151
08:31.148 --> 08:33.150
- Understood? - Understood!

152
08:33.150 --> 08:35.974
You will stay in this position until the end of training today.

153
08:35.974 --> 08:37.351
- Got it? - Yes, sir!

154
08:37.351 --> 08:40.685
- Louder. Got it? - Yes, sir!

155
09:03.223 --> 09:06.260
Is he fucking stupid?

156
09:07.894 --> 09:09.528
Fuck.

157
09:09.528 --> 09:11.438
Can you keep quiet?

158
09:11.438 --> 09:13.678
What the fuck did you say?

159
09:13.678 --> 09:16.001
You're not the only one getting smoked. It's hard for everyone.

160
09:16.001 --> 09:18.777
What the fuck are you talking about?

161
09:18.777 --> 09:20.791
What did you say?

162
09:20.791 --> 09:22.076
Hey.

163
09:22.076 --> 09:23.369
Say that again.

164
09:23.369 --> 09:24.845
- What? - You fucking bastard.

165
09:24.845 --> 09:26.633
You fucking bastard!

166
09:29.595 --> 09:30.596
Hey, hey, stop.

167
09:30.596 --> 09:31.597
Fuck you.

168
09:31.597 --> 09:33.849
Stop him!

169
09:33.849 --> 09:35.595
Go on, bastard.

170
09:35.595 --> 09:37.269
Hey, stop.

171
09:37.269 --> 09:39.219
Stop him.

172
09:40.280 --> 09:42.580
What the heck are you doing?

173
09:46.912 --> 09:47.913
Number 9.

174
09:47.913 --> 09:50.197
Trainee 9, Kwon Tae Woong.

175
09:50.197 --> 09:51.573
Number 4.

176
09:54.776 --> 09:58.154
Trainee 4, Yeom Il Hwan, sir.

177
09:58.763 --> 10:00.252
Follow me.

178
10:00.252 --> 10:01.565
Yes, sir!

179
10:12.799 --> 10:14.621
Oh, gosh.

180
10:14.621 --> 10:16.713
We're fucked. So fucked.

181
10:16.713 --> 10:20.058
We're getting smoked again because of that crazy dude.

182
10:20.058 --> 10:22.653
Hey, we should probably stay quiet.

183
10:22.653 --> 10:25.826
What kind of bullshit is this?

184
10:27.025 --> 10:29.073
It's alright.

185
10:29.073 --> 10:30.757
Nothing to worry about.

186
10:43.864 --> 10:47.186
You must have relied on each other.

187
10:47.186 --> 10:51.183
Yes, we have, back then.

188
10:52.073 --> 10:53.177
And now?

189
10:53.177 --> 10:54.889
Are you...

190
10:54.889 --> 10:56.099
Oh, no.

191
10:56.099 --> 10:57.576
We still get along well.

192
10:57.576 --> 11:01.004
I should be nice to Hyeon Uk from now on.

193
11:01.004 --> 11:03.199
- Yes. - Right.

194
11:04.120 --> 11:07.526
What ramen should I eat later?

195
11:08.954 --> 11:10.629
Well...

196
11:10.629 --> 11:12.683
Corporal Park Min Seok.

197
11:12.683 --> 11:14.332
Perhaps...

198
11:19.814 --> 11:21.326
No, it's nothing.

199
11:21.326 --> 11:23.258
Well, okay.

200
11:23.258 --> 11:25.104
Let's stay sharp on watch.

201
11:25.104 --> 11:26.989
Yes, sir.

202
11:36.342 --> 11:40.123
Look at you, short-timers. You're all here on time without your morning smoke?

203
11:40.123 --> 11:44.226
Sir, we always come out when we're supposed to. It's just this shit that won't come out!

204
11:44.226 --> 11:47.141
I got constipated here, of all places. I didn't even get it in boot camp.

205
11:47.141 --> 11:49.748
Hey, just hold out till we get Army burgers!

206
11:49.748 --> 11:51.479
They'll clear you right up.

207
11:51.479 --> 11:52.671
There. Jeon Se Gye.

208
11:52.671 --> 11:53.815
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

209
11:53.815 --> 11:55.890
Didn't you shoot a commercial before you came here?

210
11:55.890 --> 11:56.891
Yes, sir!

211
11:56.891 --> 11:59.320
"If you're constipated...

212
11:59.320 --> 12:01.560
Mayday."

213
12:01.560 --> 12:02.560
Nice.

214
12:02.560 --> 12:04.910
Everyone, about face!

215
12:06.153 --> 12:09.378
Give me a loud five-second shout!

216
12:13.074 --> 12:14.240
Okay, okay.

217
12:14.240 --> 12:16.926
Everyone, about face!

218
12:16.926 --> 12:18.852
Wow, is this the power of quitting smoking?

219
12:18.852 --> 12:21.479
Your voices sound so clear!

220
12:21.479 --> 12:23.642
Now that you all quit smoking and got healthy,

221
12:23.642 --> 12:28.120
I'll let you skip the morning run...

222
12:28.120 --> 12:29.602
Actually, no! Guide on Kim Sang Hun!

223
12:29.602 --> 12:30.918
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun, guide!

224
12:30.918 --> 12:32.788
Form up! Hurry up! Hurry!

225
12:32.788 --> 12:34.871
- One, two, hup! - One, two, hup!

226
12:36.326 --> 12:37.956
Chungseong!

227
12:42.227 --> 12:43.729
Chungseong.

228
12:43.729 --> 12:45.286
Is roll call over?

229
12:45.286 --> 12:49.720
I came out early so I could run with the guys from Second Company.

230
12:49.720 --> 12:52.167
No, sir. We were just forming up for a run.

231
12:52.167 --> 12:53.595
Then that's good.

232
12:53.595 --> 12:55.545
Let's run together.

233
12:57.612 --> 12:58.989
Run. Let's go.

234
12:58.989 --> 13:00.049
Second Company!

235
13:00.049 --> 13:02.598
The cadence is "A Fine Man!"

236
13:02.598 --> 13:03.599
Cadence start!

237
13:03.599 --> 13:05.185
One, two, three, four!

238
13:05.185 --> 13:08.376
♪ A fine man ♪

239
13:08.376 --> 13:11.070
♪ Out of many ♪

240
13:11.070 --> 13:14.635
♪ I am the man ♪

241
13:14.635 --> 13:17.685
♪ A fine man I am ♪

242
13:17.685 --> 13:18.795
Hey, Min Seok.

243
13:18.795 --> 13:20.603
You run better than I expected.

244
13:20.603 --> 13:21.608
Corporal Park Min Seok!

245
13:21.608 --> 13:24.431
Yes, sir, my stamina has increased since becoming a corporal, sir!

246
13:24.431 --> 13:26.489
Watch out for injuries, have a safe run!

247
13:26.489 --> 13:27.949
Yes, sir, thank you!

248
13:27.949 --> 13:30.323
- Good! - ♪ A fine man ♪

249
13:33.729 --> 13:35.101
- Company Commander. - Yes, sir.

250
13:35.101 --> 13:37.360
Make sure these kids get enough breakfast.

251
13:37.360 --> 13:40.726
They have civilian support duties at Yooncheon-ri today.

252
13:40.726 --> 13:42.741
But sir, it's the weekend. Isn't it too sudden?

253
13:42.741 --> 13:45.998
There are no "weekends" for operations, nor do they come announced.

254
13:45.998 --> 13:47.198
Understood, sir.

255
13:47.198 --> 13:48.810
The mayor will be there...

256
13:48.810 --> 13:51.548
The press has their eyes on it, too.

257
13:51.548 --> 13:54.581
I'd like our Second Company to make an appearance there.

258
13:54.581 --> 13:56.816
I'm sure you understand me.

259
13:56.816 --> 13:57.907
Yes, sir.

260
13:57.907 --> 13:59.376
Perfect. I expect no less from you.

261
13:59.376 --> 14:01.878
- Yes, sir. Chungseong. - ♪ A fine man ♪

262
14:01.878 --> 14:04.928
♪ Out of many ♪

263
14:13.416 --> 14:15.953
Our battalion commander's stamina is seriously impressive!

264
14:15.953 --> 14:17.713
I shouldn't have to go through this, I'm a short-timer!

265
14:17.713 --> 14:19.029
But, still...

266
14:19.029 --> 14:20.909
I think it's good exercise.

267
14:20.909 --> 14:22.387
Good? What's good about this?

268
14:22.387 --> 14:24.484
Well, I have to admit, it is refreshing.

269
14:24.484 --> 14:27.849
Weekend mornings aren't supposed to be this tiring!

270
14:29.683 --> 14:31.621
This is the admin office speaking.

271
14:31.621 --> 14:35.015
There is a civilian support mission scheduled for today at Yooncheon-ri.

272
14:35.015 --> 14:36.428
All personnel in the Second Company, without exception...

273
14:36.428 --> 14:40.334
- What? - must gather at the parade grounds by 9:00.

274
14:40.334 --> 14:41.603
A civil support mission?

275
14:41.603 --> 14:43.101
Did I just hear that correctly?

276
14:43.101 --> 14:45.641
Yes, they said "civilian support mission," loud and clear.

277
14:45.641 --> 14:46.882
But it's so sudden!

278
14:46.882 --> 14:48.734
This is so unfair, it's the weekend.

279
14:48.734 --> 14:50.700
This is unheard of, isn't it?

280
14:50.700 --> 14:52.841
Damn it, why did it have to be our company?

281
14:52.841 --> 14:56.453
Maybe the beef between the company commander and the battalion commander?

282
14:56.453 --> 14:58.369
And why did I have to get so unlucky in my last year of service?

283
14:58.369 --> 14:59.547
This sucks!

284
14:59.547 --> 15:02.021
- Come on, just hurry up and get ready. - Yes, sir!

285
15:02.021 --> 15:03.646
Get everyone ready, Min Seok.

286
15:03.646 --> 15:05.451
Got it, sir.

287
15:07.183 --> 15:09.118
Hey, Bit Na Ri, and Hyeon Uk.

288
15:09.118 --> 15:11.390
Keep your guards up even higher out there, got it?

289
15:11.390 --> 15:12.487
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

290
15:12.487 --> 15:13.923
- Hurry up. - Yes, sir.

291
15:13.923 --> 15:16.200
This is the admin office again.

292
15:16.200 --> 15:17.987
Under the battalion commander's orders,

293
15:17.987 --> 15:21.573
all personnel must change into their Class A uniform.

294
15:21.573 --> 15:23.361
I will repeat this one more time.

295
15:23.361 --> 15:25.064
Under the battalion commander's orders,

296
15:25.064 --> 15:26.939
- all personnel must wear the Class A uniform. - What?

297
15:26.939 --> 15:29.239
Why would we need to wear that for a civil support mission?

298
15:29.239 --> 15:30.523
My exact question, too.

299
15:30.523 --> 15:33.583
If we end up going shoveling or something, it's only going to ruin the uniform...

300
15:33.583 --> 15:35.079
- Wait a minute. - What if, by any chance...

301
15:35.079 --> 15:37.135
we got invited to the town festival?

302
15:37.135 --> 15:38.570
- Makgeolli? - Oh, makgeolli!

303
15:38.570 --> 15:40.649
- Makgeolli? - Makgeolli?

304
15:40.649 --> 15:42.267
- Quick, get changed! - Yes, sir!

305
15:42.267 --> 15:45.398
Maybe we're going to some municipal event!

306
15:45.398 --> 15:46.427
If so...

307
15:46.427 --> 15:49.670
there may just be some pretty college girl volunteers there as well!

308
15:49.670 --> 15:51.970
- College girls? - Oh, yes!

309
15:51.970 --> 15:54.898
Those pretty college girl volunteers...

310
15:54.898 --> 15:57.239
Hey, Bit Na Ri. Come over here.

311
15:57.239 --> 15:59.370
Those pretty college girl volunteers...

312
15:59.370 --> 16:03.255
Well, just imagine them seeing us and going... "Oh, Mr. Soldier!

313
16:03.255 --> 16:04.770
Thank you for your service!"

314
16:04.770 --> 16:05.992
And then...

315
16:05.992 --> 16:08.489
She hands you a vitamin drink...

316
16:08.489 --> 16:10.442
But then... Your hand brushes against hers...

317
16:10.442 --> 16:11.692
"Ohoho!"

318
16:11.692 --> 16:13.207
She giggles, all shy and flustered, and...

319
16:13.207 --> 16:14.659
"Oh..."

320
16:17.882 --> 16:20.544
"What strong hands you have!"

321
16:26.216 --> 16:28.816
And straight to day one it is!

322
16:39.253 --> 16:42.239
Corporal Im Da Hye, may I borrow some sunscreen?

323
16:42.239 --> 16:44.261
No way. You need to become a corporal first.

324
16:44.261 --> 16:45.617
Yes, sir...

325
16:45.617 --> 16:46.644
Hey, Bit Na Ri.

326
16:46.644 --> 16:47.917
Here you go.

327
16:47.917 --> 16:50.198
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri! Thank you, sir!

328
16:50.198 --> 16:53.139
- Go easy on it, okay? - Yes, sir!

329
16:53.139 --> 16:54.489
This is the company commander speaking.

330
16:54.489 --> 16:56.802
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye and Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

331
16:56.802 --> 16:58.892
Report to the company commander's office. Over.

332
16:58.892 --> 17:01.536
- Quick, change and get going! - Yes, sir.

333
17:03.924 --> 17:05.322
Yes?

334
17:10.218 --> 17:11.625
Chungseong! Love you!

335
17:11.625 --> 17:13.374
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye and one other,

336
17:13.374 --> 17:15.500
- reporting to the company commander's office! - Good.

337
17:15.500 --> 17:17.834
- Jeon Se Gye. - Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

338
17:17.834 --> 17:20.174
I summoned you, Se Gye and Hyeon Uk,

339
17:20.174 --> 17:23.520
to tell you that you two will be staying here.

340
17:23.520 --> 17:25.770
I'll inform your squad leaders.

341
17:27.479 --> 17:30.478
The battalion commander is worried that people may take photos of you.

342
17:30.478 --> 17:32.704
He wants you to stay behind.

343
17:33.740 --> 17:35.908
- Is that, sir? - Se Gye.

344
17:35.908 --> 17:37.916
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye.

345
17:37.916 --> 17:39.411
You are Jeon Se Gye.

346
17:39.411 --> 17:41.559
But, Company Commander, sir...

347
17:41.559 --> 17:43.410
Not a lot of people recognize me anymore, sir.

348
17:43.410 --> 17:45.622
- Not even people from other Companies do. - That's precisely why.

349
17:45.622 --> 17:49.831
We don't want gossip that you've changed, much less with photo evidence, too.

350
17:49.831 --> 17:51.252
Oh, dear.

351
17:51.252 --> 17:54.280
But, sir, it can't be that bad!

352
17:54.280 --> 17:56.034
Oh, calm down. I was just joking.

353
17:56.034 --> 17:59.022
I'm so hurt I'm on the verge of tears, see?

354
17:59.022 --> 18:00.936
Right here, do you see it, sir?

355
18:00.936 --> 18:03.261
Alright, alright. Hey, Hyeon Uk.

356
18:03.261 --> 18:04.696
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

357
18:04.696 --> 18:08.461
It hasn't been long since you were assigned, and your priority is to get used to your unit.

358
18:08.461 --> 18:10.410
- So stay behind, alright? - Yes, sir!

359
18:10.410 --> 18:12.765
- But don't take this as a vacation. - Yes, sir!

360
18:12.765 --> 18:14.087
Good.

361
18:14.087 --> 18:15.986
Okay, let's go.

362
18:16.690 --> 18:18.478
If it were up to me, I'd rather do civilian support.

363
18:18.478 --> 18:21.554
Working with the first sergeant is...

364
18:21.554 --> 18:23.028
What are you talking about?

365
18:23.028 --> 18:24.742
I'm wonderful to work with!

366
18:24.742 --> 18:26.759
Hey! I'll buy you a Buddion.

367
18:26.759 --> 18:28.819
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye, thank you, sir!

368
18:28.819 --> 18:30.502
We'll be back.

369
18:36.283 --> 18:38.444
Oh, A-class! Are you going on vacation?

370
18:38.444 --> 18:42.049
Watch and learn, nerds! This is what it means to be a cool guy!

371
18:42.835 --> 18:44.720
So, where are we going today, sir?

372
18:44.720 --> 18:48.494
I don't know, but anywhere would be better than here!

373
18:48.494 --> 18:50.843
- That's true, sir! - And there'll be college girls, no?

374
18:50.843 --> 18:51.878
I'm so excited.

375
18:51.878 --> 18:55.025
I have a feeling I might get a girlfriend today!

376
18:55.742 --> 18:59.329
I'm excited to taste some real food for once!

377
18:59.961 --> 19:01.636
To the flowery meadows, my fellow honeybees!

378
19:01.636 --> 19:04.307
- Buzz, buzz! - Buzz!

379
19:04.307 --> 19:06.581
- Let's go, baby! - Buzz, buzz!

380
19:11.631 --> 19:13.154
What the heck.

381
19:17.500 --> 19:18.887
What's this?

382
19:18.887 --> 19:22.557
This is just a plain old flood damage restoration site.

383
19:22.557 --> 19:25.109
So why did we have to dress up for this?

384
19:26.412 --> 19:28.723
Perfect weather for manual labor.

385
19:29.892 --> 19:31.269
Chungseong! Love you!

386
19:31.269 --> 19:33.332
- Love you. - Chungseong, love you.

387
19:33.332 --> 19:34.796
Yeah.

388
19:34.796 --> 19:37.291
Hey. Dressed up in A-class, huh? Are you going on vacation?

389
19:37.291 --> 19:39.172
Oh, stop making fun of us, sir.

390
19:39.172 --> 19:41.122
We used a lot of softener for these.

391
19:41.122 --> 19:43.060
So why are we wearing these, anyway?

392
19:43.060 --> 19:44.818
This wouldn't be an army if I told you, now would it?

393
19:44.818 --> 19:46.752
You just do what you're told to.

394
19:46.752 --> 19:49.481
Everyone, gather up. Let's take a group photo.

395
19:49.481 --> 19:51.313
What group photo, now, sir?

396
19:51.313 --> 19:54.194
All your mothers and girlfriends will see it.

397
19:54.194 --> 19:55.199
Come on, hurry up.

398
19:55.199 --> 19:56.838
Yes, sir.

399
19:58.109 --> 19:59.877
What did I just say? It's for your moms!

400
19:59.877 --> 20:01.171
Smile!

401
20:01.171 --> 20:02.401
Hey, Kang Chan Seok, your face...

402
20:02.401 --> 20:03.936
- Oh. That's your relaxed face, huh. - Yes, sir.

403
20:03.936 --> 20:06.230
Hey, I said smile!

404
20:06.230 --> 20:08.022
Good. On three.

405
20:08.022 --> 20:10.586
One, two, three!

406
20:10.586 --> 20:13.536
One more time. Two, three...

407
20:14.341 --> 20:16.425
Okay. We'll take 7 and 8 later.

408
20:16.425 --> 20:18.799
- Yes, sir! - Okay. Eyes on me.

409
20:18.799 --> 20:19.957
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

410
20:19.957 --> 20:21.277
You see all that debris behind me?

411
20:21.277 --> 20:22.406
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

412
20:22.406 --> 20:24.881
We're here to restore the flood damage.

413
20:24.881 --> 20:26.382
We've got lots of eyes on us, boys.

414
20:26.382 --> 20:29.238
Let's focus and get this done, and get back home as quickly as possible.

415
20:29.238 --> 20:30.825
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

416
20:30.825 --> 20:32.344
- Jong Uk. - Corporal Cha Jong Uk.

417
20:32.344 --> 20:35.141
Get the boys to hand out work gloves.

418
20:35.141 --> 20:37.539
- Yes, sir. - Go, go!

419
20:37.539 --> 20:38.818
- Yes, sir. - Going, sir.

420
20:38.818 --> 20:41.774
- Ugh, makgeolli... - I want makgeolli...

421
21:00.908 --> 21:03.217
Hey, Hyeon Uk, put your gloves on. You'll get hurt.

422
21:03.217 --> 21:05.886
- As for me, I just prefer my bare hands. - Yes, sir.

423
21:11.337 --> 21:13.653
I don't know why we don't throw this thing out.

424
21:13.653 --> 21:15.603
The army sucks.

425
21:18.227 --> 21:20.852
- Let's take a short break. - Yes, sir.

426
21:27.617 --> 21:29.546
You work so hard, sir, even during the weekend.

427
21:29.546 --> 21:31.606
Oh, but it's not just me. You're working, too.

428
21:31.606 --> 21:33.487
Let's enjoy this break and get back to it.

429
21:33.487 --> 21:34.994
Yes, sir!

430
21:38.380 --> 21:39.800
What is it?

431
21:39.800 --> 21:41.290
I sense you've got something to say.

432
21:41.290 --> 21:42.911
It's okay, you can tell me.

433
21:42.911 --> 21:44.415
It's just...

434
21:44.415 --> 21:45.865
Well, Private Jeon Se Gye...

435
21:45.865 --> 21:47.526
Seeing that you're a celebrity,

436
21:47.526 --> 21:49.752
it wouldn't be strange for you to want some kind of special treatment.

437
21:49.752 --> 21:51.187
Special treatment, huh.

438
21:51.187 --> 21:52.921
There's no such thing in the army.

439
21:52.921 --> 21:55.401
We're all soldiers, and nothing more.

440
21:55.401 --> 21:57.527
It sure seems like that isn't always the case.

441
21:58.492 --> 22:00.338
Oh? Really?

442
22:00.338 --> 22:01.851
Like who, for example?

443
22:01.851 --> 22:03.238
Oh, well...

444
22:03.238 --> 22:05.503
This isn't specifically about him, but...

445
22:05.503 --> 22:07.916
Last time, when I misfired a blank,

446
22:07.916 --> 22:11.788
if it was anyone other than Corporal Park Min Seok who was with me...

447
22:11.788 --> 22:15.164
I can't help but wonder if it still would've blown over so easily.

448
22:16.363 --> 22:20.113
So you're wondering if you got off easy because he's the division commander's son?

449
22:20.113 --> 22:21.285
Is that what you mean?

450
22:21.285 --> 22:23.233
Well, not in particular, sir.

451
22:23.233 --> 22:26.418
- I was just giving an example. - Well, that "special treatment..."

452
22:26.418 --> 22:29.020
It's not always a good thing. Sometimes it can get in your way.

453
22:29.020 --> 22:31.609
- Even if it is special? - Of course.

454
22:31.609 --> 22:33.245
Especially when...

455
22:33.245 --> 22:35.540
It wasn't even wanted.

456
22:35.540 --> 22:36.900
It's just worse.

457
22:37.665 --> 22:40.546
- Is that right? - Yeah.

458
22:40.546 --> 22:43.453
- Come on, let's get this over with. - Yes, sir!

459
22:50.766 --> 22:52.070
What's wrong?

460
22:52.070 --> 22:54.979
Let me guess. You're wondering why we put in all this effort when there's no one around?

461
22:54.979 --> 22:56.029
That's correct, sir.

462
22:56.029 --> 22:58.344
It doesn't matter if there's anyone around or not, does it?

463
22:58.344 --> 23:00.697
You're just supposed to do your best on the task at hand.

464
23:00.697 --> 23:02.509
I'm surprised to hear that from a celebrity.

465
23:02.509 --> 23:04.232
Hey, I may be a celebrity in the outside world,

466
23:04.232 --> 23:06.292
but here, we're all the same. Just soldiers.

467
23:06.292 --> 23:07.899
It's just that I'm a little...

468
23:07.899 --> 23:10.626
No, more than a little, dare I say, very...

469
23:10.626 --> 23:12.992
handsome soldier.

470
23:12.992 --> 23:14.812
You're right, sir!

471
23:17.201 --> 23:19.803
W-wait a second.

472
23:29.872 --> 23:31.335
[Buddion]

473
23:32.682 --> 23:35.989
I noticed the poor thing, stuck there all alone.

474
23:38.505 --> 23:40.506
- Do you want it? - I'm all right, sir!

475
23:40.506 --> 23:43.501
- No, take it. - It's seriously alright, sir.

476
23:43.501 --> 23:45.690
- You mean that? - Yes, sir.

477
23:51.817 --> 23:53.521
Oh, I'm getting a signal right away.

478
23:53.521 --> 23:54.865
I need to use the restroom.

479
23:54.865 --> 23:55.920
Yes, sir.

480
23:55.920 --> 23:58.280
Why don't you come with me? You haven't gone even once.

481
23:58.280 --> 23:59.321
I'm good, sir!

482
23:59.321 --> 24:00.758
You sure? Alright then, I'll be back.

483
24:00.758 --> 24:02.483
Yes, sir!

484
24:19.878 --> 24:21.810
- What are you doing? - I'm fine, sir.

485
24:21.810 --> 24:23.344
See the bucket there?

486
24:23.344 --> 24:25.156
- Hey, stop! Stop. - Stop.

487
24:25.156 --> 24:26.157
Good.

488
24:26.157 --> 24:27.410
Okay, smile!

489
24:27.410 --> 24:28.411
Okay.

490
24:28.411 --> 24:30.275
One, two, three.

491
24:30.275 --> 24:32.179
Smile. With your teeth.

492
24:32.179 --> 24:35.214
- Yes, sir. - Wipe away a little sweat.

493
24:35.214 --> 24:37.183
Okay, okay.

494
24:37.183 --> 24:39.117
Hurry up.

495
24:39.117 --> 24:40.723
Okay.

496
24:40.723 --> 24:42.648
Hey, come here.

497
24:42.648 --> 24:44.067
Look at you sweating.

498
24:44.067 --> 24:46.320
What's keeping you? Come over here.

499
24:46.320 --> 24:47.385
Sorry, sir.

500
24:47.385 --> 24:49.455
Watch out.

501
24:49.455 --> 24:50.456
Nice, nice.

502
24:50.456 --> 24:52.939
[Cyber Knowledge Information Room]

503
24:59.167 --> 25:01.814
You're back, sir.

504
25:01.814 --> 25:03.155
Let's get it done quickly and go to the post exchange.

505
25:03.155 --> 25:04.492
Sounds great, sir.

506
25:04.492 --> 25:07.093
Private First Class Jeon Se Gye. May I use the restroom?

507
25:07.093 --> 25:08.172
Sure, go ahead.

508
25:08.172 --> 25:09.809
Thank you, sir.

509
25:14.258 --> 25:16.293
We're almost done. Cheer up.

510
25:16.293 --> 25:17.935
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

511
25:17.935 --> 25:19.391
Hey, sweep there properly.

512
25:19.391 --> 25:20.436
Yes, sir.

513
25:20.436 --> 25:22.272
- Don't sweep this way. - Fine.

514
25:22.272 --> 25:23.804
At ease!

515
25:24.775 --> 25:26.972
Company, attention!

516
25:29.294 --> 25:31.364
Chungseong! Love you!

517
25:31.364 --> 25:33.814
Chungseong. Love you.

518
25:33.814 --> 25:34.815
At ease.

519
25:34.815 --> 25:36.195
At ease!

520
25:36.195 --> 25:39.017
- Do what you were doing. - Yes, sir!

521
25:39.655 --> 25:40.656
Corporal Park Min Seok.

522
25:40.656 --> 25:41.657
Corporal Park Min Seok.

523
25:41.657 --> 25:44.944
- You're working hard. - It's nothing, sir. Thank you, sir.

524
25:44.944 --> 25:50.523
Reporters, please feel free to interview them from now on.

525
25:50.523 --> 25:52.907
I'd appreciate it if you could give us some good coverage.

526
25:52.907 --> 25:54.926
Please come this way.

527
25:56.959 --> 25:59.678
Did you all enjoy breakfast?

528
25:59.678 --> 26:01.253
Corporal Cha Jong Uk. Yes, we did, sir.

529
26:01.253 --> 26:04.494
What's the most important thing when we work?

530
26:04.494 --> 26:05.697
It's being safe.

531
26:05.697 --> 26:07.575
Yes, sir.

532
26:07.575 --> 26:09.372
Yes, sir.

533
26:19.289 --> 26:21.439
Sang Hun, here.

534
26:27.529 --> 26:30.380
- Second Company, attention! - Attention.

535
26:30.380 --> 26:32.767
- Attention! - Attention!

536
26:32.767 --> 26:35.336
I appreciate your hard work in this heat.

537
26:35.336 --> 26:38.327
What we are doing here is

538
26:38.327 --> 26:44.324
helping heal the hearts of the people of Yooncheon-ri, devastated by the flood.

539
26:44.324 --> 26:46.021
But...

540
26:46.021 --> 26:49.428
why do you think I, your battalion commander,

541
26:49.428 --> 26:52.601
ordered you to wear your Class A uniforms in this mud?

542
26:54.286 --> 26:55.287
Well...

543
26:55.287 --> 26:56.388
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

544
26:56.388 --> 26:58.315
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

545
26:58.315 --> 27:00.233
What do you think the reason is?

546
27:01.019 --> 27:02.020
Because they are clean, sir!

547
27:02.020 --> 27:03.779
Come on.

548
27:05.425 --> 27:07.878
Yes, that's not wrong.

549
27:07.878 --> 27:10.083
If we wear fatigues,

550
27:10.083 --> 27:14.110
that means we're just here to lend a hand.

551
27:14.110 --> 27:18.972
But when we stand here in these spotless uniforms,

552
27:18.972 --> 27:21.565
that means

553
27:21.565 --> 27:26.243
we are here as the very safety our country has promised.

554
27:26.859 --> 27:28.978
Right now,

555
27:30.800 --> 27:34.591
you are the finest Class A rescue force

556
27:34.591 --> 27:37.247
our country has sent!

557
27:42.194 --> 27:43.339
Do you understand?

558
27:43.339 --> 27:44.864
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

559
27:44.864 --> 27:46.576
Alright, let's keep it up!

560
27:46.576 --> 27:47.695
Back to your position!

561
27:47.695 --> 27:49.856
- Yes, sir! - Yes, sir!

562
27:53.539 --> 27:56.054
Our battalion commander is awesome.

563
27:56.054 --> 27:57.055
Class A.

564
27:57.055 --> 27:58.062
Rescue force.

565
27:58.062 --> 28:00.923
I almost cried.

566
28:01.786 --> 28:02.787
Let's get to work.

567
28:02.787 --> 28:04.843
- Yes, sir! - Sorry, sir!

568
28:05.752 --> 28:07.853
Have you had breakfast?

569
28:07.853 --> 28:09.229
- Yes, we have, sir. - Yes, we have, sir.

570
28:09.229 --> 28:10.837
Alright, stay safe.

571
28:10.837 --> 28:12.319
You're here, Baek Ho. Chungseong!

572
28:12.319 --> 28:14.508
Oh, chief. Chungseong.

573
28:14.508 --> 28:17.281
I haven't seen you in a while, and you've gotten so thin!

574
28:17.281 --> 28:19.081
What are you talking about? I gained weight.

575
28:19.081 --> 28:20.082
You did?

576
28:20.082 --> 28:22.673
Hello, sir. I'm sorry I didn't get a chance to introduce myself sooner.

577
28:22.673 --> 28:25.567
I'm Lieutenant Colonel Byeon Hyeok Jin, newly assigned here.

578
28:25.567 --> 28:29.252
What? You look younger than Baek Ho, and you're already a lieutenant colonel?

579
28:29.252 --> 28:31.119
Oh, not at all.

580
28:31.119 --> 28:33.332
What have you been doing so far, not getting promoted?

581
28:33.332 --> 28:35.570
I didn't have time to get promoted because I was busy taking care of you, chief.

582
28:35.570 --> 28:37.643
That's nonsense.

583
28:44.685 --> 28:47.017
Corporal No Hee Jeong. We have a big problem.

584
28:47.017 --> 28:49.588
I'm going to kill you for real this time if it's not a big deal.

585
28:49.588 --> 28:52.065
I mean it. This is a huge problem.

586
28:52.065 --> 28:53.995
What is it?

587
28:55.915 --> 28:58.436
Damn it. It is huge.

588
28:58.436 --> 29:01.099
What should we do?

589
29:01.099 --> 29:03.030
Communication security. Corporal No Hee Jeong speaking.

590
29:03.030 --> 29:04.318
Communication security. Corporal Sung Yoon Mo speaking.

591
29:04.318 --> 29:05.621
- I'll check that for you. - How may I assist you?

592
29:05.621 --> 29:07.768
Copy. Chungseong!

593
29:07.768 --> 29:09.923
Communication security. Corporal No Hee Jeong speaking.

594
29:09.923 --> 29:11.327
Hey, what's up?

595
29:11.327 --> 29:13.402
Chungseong, Battalion Commander...

596
29:13.402 --> 29:14.425
What is it?

597
29:14.425 --> 29:17.507
Someone posted on the base forum

598
29:17.507 --> 29:20.609
[Shinhwa Unit Is Covering Up a Shooting!] that our battalion covered up a shooting.

599
29:20.609 --> 29:23.977
We're getting calls from everywhere. It's chaos.

600
29:23.977 --> 29:25.737
[Measures against the false accusation online] He's on civilian support duty now.

601
29:25.737 --> 29:28.069
[All commanders exercise extra caution] I'll get back to you, sir.

602
29:28.069 --> 29:29.318
Please hold for a second.

603
29:29.318 --> 29:30.319
Communication security. Corporal Sung Yoon Mo speaking.

604
29:30.319 --> 29:32.466
Communication security. Corporal No Hee Jeong speaking.

605
29:32.466 --> 29:34.711
Yes, he's out on duty.

606
29:34.711 --> 29:37.111
Damn it.

607
29:37.111 --> 29:38.842
Hang up for now.

608
29:40.325 --> 29:42.300
[Regimental Commander Kwon Sang Guk]

609
29:43.235 --> 29:45.008
- Chungseong. - You, bastard.

610
29:45.008 --> 29:47.343
- What the fuck are you doing? - I'm sorry, sir.

611
29:47.343 --> 29:49.752
Get your ass to regimental headquarters right now!

612
29:49.752 --> 29:51.702
Yes, sir. Chung--

613
29:57.583 --> 29:59.533
- Second Company Commander. - Yes.

614
30:00.793 --> 30:05.177
Something came up, so I should head back now.

615
30:05.177 --> 30:06.375
Can you wrap it up here?

616
30:06.375 --> 30:08.250
Yes, sir. If you don't mind...

617
30:08.250 --> 30:09.773
Did something happen?

618
30:09.773 --> 30:13.282
Well, I'll tell you when you finish here and get back to base.

619
30:13.282 --> 30:16.023
Yes, sir. Chungseong.

620
30:16.023 --> 30:17.024
Open it.

621
30:22.738 --> 30:24.863
Take it easy.

622
30:26.930 --> 30:29.033
I'll throw it away.

623
30:33.405 --> 30:34.820
Next.

624
30:34.820 --> 30:36.842
You're spilling it all.

625
30:38.045 --> 30:40.799
It's going everywhere.

626
30:47.555 --> 30:48.725
- Hey. - Yes?

627
30:48.725 --> 30:52.914
You're way stronger than you look.

628
30:52.914 --> 30:54.342
Thank you, ma'am.

629
30:54.342 --> 30:55.634
Let's go.

630
30:55.634 --> 30:57.887
Go where?

631
30:57.887 --> 31:01.888
The wall around my house completely collapsed.

632
31:01.888 --> 31:04.015
Can you mend it?

633
31:04.015 --> 31:06.032
It looks like the whole place is about to wash away!

634
31:06.032 --> 31:09.579
Ma'am, I am sorry, but I'm on duty here.

635
31:11.959 --> 31:12.960
Is that so?

636
31:12.960 --> 31:15.675
Well, then, it can't be helped.

637
31:15.675 --> 31:17.335
I'll do it on my own.

638
31:17.335 --> 31:19.188
I might end up crushed under a rock.

639
31:19.188 --> 31:21.385
- You can come get my body then. - No...

640
31:21.385 --> 31:24.810
When the soul's gone, the body will be light as a feather.

641
31:24.810 --> 31:26.538
- It'll be easy to clean up. - Ma'am...

642
31:26.538 --> 31:27.617
It's not like that, ma'am...

643
31:27.617 --> 31:28.618
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin.

644
31:28.618 --> 31:30.212
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin.

645
31:30.212 --> 31:32.871
The key to civilian support is responding to the needs on the ground.

646
31:32.871 --> 31:35.146
Go help the lady.

647
31:39.437 --> 31:40.500
Yes, sir!

648
31:40.500 --> 31:41.684
Huh?

649
31:41.684 --> 31:43.006
As a Class A rescue force,

650
31:43.006 --> 31:44.978
I, First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin, will return after fixing her wall--

651
31:44.978 --> 31:46.772
- Got it, on your way. - Yes, yes.

652
31:46.772 --> 31:49.374
- Chungseong! I will... - Let's go.

653
31:49.374 --> 31:51.905
- Thank you. - Of course.

654
31:51.905 --> 31:53.465
Take good care of her.

655
31:53.465 --> 31:55.536
Be careful, ma'am.

656
31:55.536 --> 31:57.750
- Waste no time. Take good care of her. - You got this!

657
31:57.750 --> 31:59.203
Safe way there.

658
31:59.203 --> 32:00.533
Good luck.

659
32:00.533 --> 32:02.277
My, she came all the way down here.

660
32:02.277 --> 32:03.462
Who is she?

661
32:03.462 --> 32:05.321
She lives on the hillside over there.

662
32:05.321 --> 32:07.592
She does that to every young man she sees.

663
32:07.592 --> 32:09.742
Is there a story behind this?

664
32:11.223 --> 32:14.174
The thing is, she...

665
32:19.370 --> 32:21.408
[Report on malicious post regarding the camp]

666
32:21.408 --> 32:22.818
[Online circulation status / Background]

667
32:22.818 --> 32:25.811
[A post titled "Shinhwa Unit Covering Up a Shooting" began circulating online]

668
32:25.811 --> 32:27.899
Regimental Commander, this was not a shooting.

669
32:27.899 --> 32:30.062
During a safety inspection after returning to the post,

670
32:30.062 --> 32:32.015
a minor accidental discharge of a blank round occurred.

671
32:32.015 --> 32:34.362
Does it matter if it's a live round or a blank?

672
32:34.362 --> 32:35.688
To civilians,

673
32:35.688 --> 32:39.182
fire coming out of a gun means a shooting!

674
32:39.182 --> 32:42.551
And once you say "cover-up,"

675
32:42.551 --> 32:47.554
the media will come running. Got it?

676
32:47.554 --> 32:48.599
I'm sorry, sir.

677
32:48.599 --> 32:51.351
I'll get this resolved as quickly as possible. I'll take care of it.

678
32:51.351 --> 32:53.635
You know what will happen if it goes out of control?

679
32:53.635 --> 32:55.432
I do, sir.

680
32:55.432 --> 32:58.745
Write the incident report for Division Headquarters yourself and bring it to me by tomorrow.

681
32:58.745 --> 33:00.148
Get out!

682
33:00.148 --> 33:01.548
Yes, sir.

683
33:01.548 --> 33:02.960
Chungseong.

684
33:02.960 --> 33:04.742
[Press vehicle]

685
33:04.742 --> 33:07.141
Guard Commander. Why is MBS here?

686
33:07.141 --> 33:08.613
That's what I'm saying.

687
33:08.613 --> 33:10.460
[May this youth shine for the motherland!] What would they be here for?

688
33:10.460 --> 33:11.997
Did something happen to Jeon Se Gye?

689
33:11.997 --> 33:13.313
Maybe they're here for an interview.

690
33:13.313 --> 33:15.260
Should I go and ask them?

691
33:15.260 --> 33:17.473
- Hang on a second. - If we could enter...

692
33:17.473 --> 33:20.610
Communication security. Chungseong. Staff Sergeant Oh Se Ho, Guard Commander.

693
33:20.610 --> 33:23.478
MBS is at the main gate right now.

694
33:23.478 --> 33:25.254
What are they here for?

695
33:32.353 --> 33:34.763
[Defense Daily Reporter Yoon]

696
33:34.763 --> 33:38.250
[Regimental Commander's Office]

697
33:38.250 --> 33:39.351
Oh, Mr. Yoon!

698
33:39.351 --> 33:41.581
I was meaning to talk to you.

699
33:41.581 --> 33:45.318
You called me because of that post on the base forum?

700
33:46.603 --> 33:48.644
You always get the news fast.

701
33:48.644 --> 33:51.972
You know what, how about we meet in person and have a talk?

702
34:01.324 --> 34:04.393
Did a wild boar ram into it?

703
34:04.393 --> 34:06.671
- Ma'am. - Yes?

704
34:06.671 --> 34:12.333
Even as an elite soldier in the top 10%, no, 5% in terms of combat and physical ability,

705
34:12.333 --> 34:15.371
this is more than I can handle on my own...

706
34:16.042 --> 34:18.930
If you can't do it, forget it.

707
34:18.930 --> 34:21.568
I could try moving those heavy rocks alone,

708
34:21.568 --> 34:23.051
even though I might break my back.

709
34:23.051 --> 34:24.658
I could die from that, but that's okay.

710
34:24.658 --> 34:27.410
- That's not what I'm saying. - It's not like I have anything else to do.

711
34:27.410 --> 34:28.566
I might as well die.

712
34:28.566 --> 34:30.043
No, no, ma'am.

713
34:30.043 --> 34:32.509
I'll do it. I can do it.

714
34:48.274 --> 34:50.415
Come on, put some muscle into it!

715
34:50.415 --> 34:54.887
What's wrong with you? Oh, you are weaker than I thought.

716
34:54.887 --> 34:57.755
You put it there earlier.

717
34:58.608 --> 35:01.296
Look, it doesn't fit.

718
35:01.296 --> 35:03.520
- It... - It needs to be a tight fit.

719
35:03.520 --> 35:06.190
But ma'am, it'll take longer to find one that fits perfectly.

720
35:06.190 --> 35:08.504
Don't you talk back to me, young man.

721
35:08.504 --> 35:10.472
Sorry, ma'am.

722
35:13.322 --> 35:14.940
You're being too slow!

723
35:14.940 --> 35:17.580
I don't want to do this anymore.

724
35:17.580 --> 35:18.987
Good job, there you go.

725
35:18.987 --> 35:21.369
Oh, goodness gracious!

726
35:21.369 --> 35:23.847
Well, aren't you clumsy!

727
35:23.847 --> 35:26.080
I thought they fed their soldiers well in the army these days,

728
35:26.080 --> 35:28.013
so why are you so weak?

729
35:28.013 --> 35:30.936
Are they starving you or something?

730
35:30.936 --> 35:31.937
I'm getting lightheaded...

731
35:31.937 --> 35:33.284
Look, it's sticking out right there!

732
35:33.284 --> 35:35.933
It'll collapse if you do it like that!

733
35:36.943 --> 35:39.483
- My hemoglobin is spiking-- - Don't talk back.

734
35:39.483 --> 35:41.336
Just do it.

735
35:42.934 --> 35:44.965
My task ends at stacking these back up again...

736
35:44.965 --> 35:47.876
- But never mind, anything else, ma'am? - What?

737
35:49.733 --> 35:52.240
- Here, these, too. - Okay.

738
35:52.240 --> 35:53.573
Hey, hey, hey!

739
35:53.573 --> 35:55.742
That's my darn cane!

740
36:00.713 --> 36:02.835
- I'm sorry, ma'am. - Yes, yes. Whatever.

741
36:09.898 --> 36:12.852
What difference is there between this and constructing a fort in the mountains, huh?

742
36:12.852 --> 36:14.790
I thought you said "outside air" is healing on its own?

743
36:14.790 --> 36:16.710
Have fun breathing.

744
36:16.710 --> 36:17.984
Hey, you.

745
36:17.984 --> 36:19.575
Shut up and hurry up.

746
36:19.575 --> 36:20.784
I want to go back fast.

747
36:20.784 --> 36:22.182
Yes, sir.

748
36:22.182 --> 36:24.394
Always hounding on me...

749
36:40.073 --> 36:41.974
What are you doing?

750
36:41.974 --> 36:44.617
It's not even that heavy.

751
36:49.864 --> 36:51.518
- Oh, no! - Deary me!

752
36:51.518 --> 36:52.785
Oh, what a disaster!

753
36:52.785 --> 36:56.865
- I'm so sorry, ma'am! - The whole year's worth of efforts, gone!

754
36:56.865 --> 36:59.606
Why are you fondling it? Just leave the damn thing alone!

755
36:59.606 --> 37:01.746
- But it's such a waste! - Hey, prick!

756
37:01.746 --> 37:03.273
Get down here and change.

757
37:03.273 --> 37:05.013
We still have lots of work to get through.

758
37:05.013 --> 37:06.577
What a mess you've made, you idiot.

759
37:06.577 --> 37:07.667
But I don't have anything to change into.

760
37:07.667 --> 37:10.630
Who cares? Get back down here right now!

761
37:10.630 --> 37:13.396
Hey, make sure the chickens are comfortable enough.

762
37:13.396 --> 37:16.695
Make it soft and cushioned, okay? Spread it out evenly.

763
37:16.695 --> 37:18.506
- Soft and cushioned... - Yes, evenly.

764
37:18.506 --> 37:20.792
Hey, could you step out of the way?

765
37:20.792 --> 37:22.645
They're breeding hens.

766
37:22.645 --> 37:25.314
Very valuable, alright? They need good care.

767
37:25.314 --> 37:27.110
Ah, yes, ma'am.

768
37:31.627 --> 37:35.086
Oh, my. It's just a chicken. Nothing to be scared of.

769
37:35.086 --> 37:37.233
Go, get out!

770
37:37.233 --> 37:40.034
What kind of a soldier gets so scared of a chicken?

771
37:40.034 --> 37:41.359
The chicken's feet are too big!

772
37:41.359 --> 37:43.471
What are you even talking about?

773
37:43.471 --> 37:45.565
You're such a funny guy.

774
37:47.122 --> 37:49.472
They're making weird noises.

775
38:00.862 --> 38:02.044
Hey.

776
38:02.044 --> 38:03.290
Come over here.

777
38:03.290 --> 38:04.291
Yes?

778
38:04.291 --> 38:06.843
Come take a look at the light here in the kitchen.

779
38:06.843 --> 38:10.209
It flickered for a few minutes, and then it turned off.

780
38:10.209 --> 38:11.413
The light?

781
38:11.413 --> 38:13.138
Yes.

782
38:14.738 --> 38:18.708
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin. I'll fix it up right away for you.

783
38:26.150 --> 38:30.141
What is it? Are you going to fix it or not?

784
38:30.141 --> 38:33.344
What are you doing, just looking at it?

785
38:33.344 --> 38:34.807
Ma'am.

786
38:34.807 --> 38:36.808
- This is more than just changing the bulb. - What?

787
38:36.808 --> 38:41.240
The electrical system in this house is estimated to date back to the 1960s or 1970s.

788
38:41.240 --> 38:44.550
The copper in the wiring has oxidized, significantly reducing its conductivity.

789
38:44.550 --> 38:49.707
In addition, worn-out insulation and sheathing could cause electrical leakage at any time.

790
38:49.707 --> 38:52.117
What the hell are you babbling about?

791
38:52.117 --> 38:54.191
I'm saying it's dangerous.

792
38:54.191 --> 38:55.420
And it's very dangerous.

793
38:55.420 --> 38:59.300
If I were to come into direct contact with this exposed wire,

794
38:59.300 --> 39:01.442
my body would become a conductor connected to the ground--

795
39:01.442 --> 39:02.579
Shut it!

796
39:02.579 --> 39:04.468
Leave it if you can't do it.

797
39:04.468 --> 39:08.984
Even if something goes wrong, I'll just get electrocuted and die, won't I?

798
39:08.984 --> 39:10.014
- Right? - No...

799
39:10.014 --> 39:15.222
With someone here to haul my body away, I feel like I'm in good hands.

800
39:15.222 --> 39:19.522
My body will go stiff when I get electrocuted, so it will be easy to move.

801
39:19.522 --> 39:21.857
Must be nice and easy to put in a coffin, too.

802
39:21.857 --> 39:24.938
Ma'am, why do you keep saying such things?

803
39:24.938 --> 39:27.188
Fine, I'll do it.

804
39:27.960 --> 39:29.392
I studied humanities...

805
39:29.392 --> 39:31.747
- What? - It's nothing.

806
39:36.607 --> 39:38.802
- Oh? - Oh, ma'am.

807
39:38.802 --> 39:42.427
I think I can do this. I found what caused the problem.

808
39:42.427 --> 39:44.812
If you put them together...

809
39:47.493 --> 39:48.737
What was that noise?

810
39:48.737 --> 39:52.318
What was that? Was that a water deer?

811
39:52.318 --> 39:53.768
Wasn't it more like a scream?

812
39:53.768 --> 39:55.408
You're just imagining it.

813
39:55.408 --> 39:57.645
Well, you did a good job today.

814
39:57.645 --> 39:59.202
- Thank you, sir. - Thank you, sir.

815
39:59.202 --> 40:02.551
- You guys must be hungry. - Yes, sir!

816
40:02.551 --> 40:04.052
It's about time.

817
40:04.052 --> 40:05.681
I'm starving. What's for dinner today?

818
40:05.681 --> 40:07.969
Stir-fried sausages and vegetables, seaweed soup, and seasoned laver...

819
40:07.969 --> 40:09.769
Delivery!

820
40:09.769 --> 40:11.215
Delivery?

821
40:11.215 --> 40:12.800
Did anyone order jjajangmyeon here?

822
40:12.800 --> 40:14.463
- What? - That sounds yummy.

823
40:14.463 --> 40:16.133
Did anyone order jjajangmyeon?

824
40:16.133 --> 40:17.466
Here.

825
40:17.466 --> 40:18.535
Oh?

826
40:18.535 --> 40:19.635
What?

827
40:19.635 --> 40:21.102
- Is this for real? - Wow!

828
40:24.425 --> 40:25.904
Calm down, calm down.

829
40:25.904 --> 40:27.905
You deserve this for your hard work.

830
40:27.905 --> 40:29.797
- Am I right? - Yes, sir!

831
40:29.797 --> 40:31.908
Company, attention!

832
40:31.908 --> 40:36.854
To our gracious, merciful, handsome, and magnificent company commander, salute!

833
40:36.854 --> 40:38.819
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

834
40:38.819 --> 40:40.852
Chungseong. Love you.

835
40:43.858 --> 40:46.321
They're all large portions.

836
40:48.121 --> 40:50.814
Fried dumplings are on the house!

837
40:52.749 --> 40:53.850
You silly bastards.

838
40:53.850 --> 40:57.184
- Salute! - Chungseong! Love you!

839
40:57.184 --> 40:59.328
I'm sorry about these guys.

840
40:59.328 --> 41:01.353
Get one each.

841
41:02.641 --> 41:03.842
Pass it back.

842
41:03.842 --> 41:05.517
To the back.

843
41:06.344 --> 41:08.562
Slow down, you'll choke.

844
41:08.562 --> 41:10.971
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

845
41:16.199 --> 41:17.225
Why are you not eating?

846
41:17.225 --> 41:18.520
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri.

847
41:18.520 --> 41:20.470
I already finished it.

848
41:21.252 --> 41:22.897
You're number one in the company at this.

849
41:22.897 --> 41:24.547
Thank you, sir!

850
41:32.157 --> 41:33.158
Do you want more?

851
41:33.158 --> 41:35.454
U-Uh, no, sir!

852
41:35.454 --> 41:36.865
No? I was going to share with you if you wanted.

853
41:36.865 --> 41:38.815
In fact, I do, sir.

854
41:39.566 --> 41:42.076
Then you should have said that. Here.

855
41:42.076 --> 41:44.101
Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri. Thank you, sir!

856
41:44.101 --> 41:45.359
Company Commander, I love you!

857
41:45.359 --> 41:46.731
Sure. Take your time.

858
41:46.731 --> 41:48.378
Yes, sir.

859
41:53.929 --> 41:55.455
Can I have a bite?

860
41:55.455 --> 41:58.339
- Yes, sir. - Thank you.

861
42:01.017 --> 42:02.723
Bro.

862
42:02.723 --> 42:05.777
When we finish this jjajangmyeon, we'll crave a cigarette badly, won't we?

863
42:05.777 --> 42:07.509
I wasn't thinking about it.

864
42:07.509 --> 42:08.780
You just made me think of it.

865
42:08.780 --> 42:10.343
I feel so empty.

866
42:10.343 --> 42:12.491
- Oh, right. - Yummy.

867
42:12.491 --> 42:14.578
- Pass this back. - Yes, sir.

868
42:16.528 --> 42:18.054
Pass along.

869
42:18.816 --> 42:19.925
It's good.

870
42:19.925 --> 42:21.222
Don't forget to drink water.

871
42:21.222 --> 42:22.834
Thank you, sir.

872
42:22.834 --> 42:24.916
What's with the sudden volunteer work?

873
42:24.916 --> 42:25.917
Enjoy while you can.

874
42:25.917 --> 42:27.094
You, too.

875
42:27.094 --> 42:28.647
- Corporal Cha Byeong Ho. - Alright.

876
42:28.647 --> 42:31.328
- Private First Class Moon Bit Na Ri. - Yes, Na Ri.

877
42:31.328 --> 42:32.831
You too.

878
42:32.831 --> 42:33.832
Thank you, sir.

879
42:33.832 --> 42:37.169
- Sergeant Kim Sang Hun. Thank you, sir. - Thank you, sir.

880
42:37.169 --> 42:38.514
- You too, Da Hye. - Corporal Im Da Hye.

881
42:38.514 --> 42:39.515
There you go.

882
42:39.515 --> 42:41.348
How sweet.

883
42:45.173 --> 42:47.708
Attention while seated!

884
42:48.558 --> 42:54.234
To our gracious, merciful, handsome, and magnificent company commander, salute!

885
42:54.234 --> 42:56.066
- Chungseong! Love you! - Chungseong! Love you!

886
42:56.066 --> 42:57.337
Chungseong. Love you.

887
42:57.337 --> 42:59.590
You silly guys. Stop it now!

888
42:59.590 --> 43:02.340
Here, pour for yourself.

889
43:05.601 --> 43:07.699
Yes, First Sergeant.

890
43:07.699 --> 43:10.649
Is something going on at the unit?

891
43:11.852 --> 43:13.101
Sorry?

892
43:18.537 --> 43:21.071
Did you fix it, ma'am?

893
43:21.071 --> 43:23.865
I flipped the breaker, you idiot!

894
43:23.865 --> 43:27.256
What kind of man can't even handle a little electrical work?

895
43:27.256 --> 43:29.872
You knocked out the power to the whole house.

896
43:29.872 --> 43:32.203
Then you just flopped down to take a break.

897
43:32.203 --> 43:33.603
Must be comfortable.

898
43:33.603 --> 43:34.656
Ma'am...

899
43:34.656 --> 43:37.578
Electricity is like an invisible enemy.

900
43:37.578 --> 43:42.106
The wiring in this traditional house uses outdated standards from the 1960s and 1970s.

901
43:42.106 --> 43:46.263
Its insulation resistance is dangerously low, with a high risk of fire and electric shock.

902
43:46.263 --> 43:49.185
Next time you need to fix a light, call a professional--

903
43:49.185 --> 43:50.803
Shut it already.

904
43:50.803 --> 43:54.816
Shut up and eat this so you feel better.

905
43:54.816 --> 43:56.520
When did you make this?

906
43:56.520 --> 43:57.636
The power wasn't even on.

907
43:57.636 --> 44:01.475
I can make this even with my eyes closed.

908
44:01.475 --> 44:02.852
Eat up.

909
44:02.852 --> 44:06.113
You need to feel better to move the rocks.

910
44:06.113 --> 44:09.650
- I thought I moved all the rocks earlier-- - What?

911
44:09.650 --> 44:11.328
Nothing, ma'am.

912
44:11.328 --> 44:13.806
Oh, but this looks like a lot.

913
44:13.806 --> 44:17.078
I've been watching my diet lately. If I eat all this, my blood sugar will...

914
44:18.135 --> 44:20.117
Thank you for preparing it.

915
44:21.311 --> 44:23.142
Wow.

916
44:23.142 --> 44:25.201
It looks yummy, very hearty...

917
44:32.730 --> 44:33.900
Are you not eating?

918
44:33.900 --> 44:37.530
No, I just prepare food like this every day.

919
44:37.530 --> 44:38.531
Go ahead and eat.

920
44:38.531 --> 44:40.105
Yes, ma'am.

921
44:40.105 --> 44:41.707
It's a little too strong for me, though.

922
44:41.707 --> 44:42.708
- Strong? - No.

923
44:42.708 --> 44:45.305
- Too strong? - No, it's not.

924
44:45.305 --> 44:47.967
My family usually seasons food pretty heavily at home, too.

925
44:48.912 --> 44:50.585
Thank you for the food.

926
45:00.797 --> 45:02.694
Oh, my.

927
45:02.694 --> 45:06.522
You cleaned your bowl without leaving a drop of sauce!

928
45:06.522 --> 45:08.076
Here, eat some more.

929
45:08.076 --> 45:10.519
No, ma'am, hold on a second.

930
45:10.519 --> 45:11.970
I'm already full.

931
45:11.970 --> 45:13.570
If you don't want it, it's fine.

932
45:13.570 --> 45:15.335
I can just throw it all away.

933
45:15.335 --> 45:17.122
No, don't! I'll eat.

934
45:17.122 --> 45:19.011
Will you?

935
45:19.011 --> 45:20.947
Thank you.

936
45:20.947 --> 45:21.948
Wow.

937
45:21.948 --> 45:24.089
It looks yummier, heartier...

938
45:41.405 --> 45:43.243
Who is that?

939
45:43.976 --> 45:45.415
Doesn't he look good?

940
45:45.415 --> 45:47.565
It's my youngest son.

941
45:51.599 --> 45:52.827
Oh, my.

942
45:52.827 --> 45:54.317
Dear.

943
45:54.317 --> 45:59.424
He used to like noodles a lot.

944
45:59.424 --> 46:01.102
I didn't know you had a son.

945
46:01.102 --> 46:05.751
It might have been better if you asked your son to change the light bulb...

946
46:05.751 --> 46:08.426
Oh, then this must be for your son, too.

947
46:08.426 --> 46:13.120
It gets lonely, so I always set the table for both of us.

948
46:13.120 --> 46:15.621
But noodles will get soggy. It's better to cook when he's here.

949
46:15.621 --> 46:17.843
Soggy or not, it doesn't matter.

950
46:17.843 --> 46:20.561
He can't eat it anyway.

951
46:32.250 --> 46:34.180
Your son...

952
46:36.093 --> 46:38.874
He's probably somewhere far away.

953
46:41.143 --> 46:44.534
Maybe somewhere in the sky.

954
46:54.858 --> 46:57.858
Maybe she brought me here because I reminded her of her son.

955
46:57.858 --> 47:03.479
Well, you reminded me of my son.

956
47:04.118 --> 47:05.955
This rascal...

957
47:05.955 --> 47:10.818
He used to love noodles.

958
47:16.187 --> 47:18.227
Ma'am.

959
47:18.227 --> 47:19.768
Is it okay if I eat this too?

960
47:19.768 --> 47:22.364
Sure, go ahead.

961
47:28.057 --> 47:30.707
My little Chang Ju...

962
47:30.707 --> 47:33.012
You must be full.

963
47:33.645 --> 47:37.105
Someone's here to enjoy it for you.

964
47:39.811 --> 47:41.961
It's really good.

965
47:43.214 --> 47:47.638
These are the best noodles I've ever had.

966
48:08.585 --> 48:12.368
Oh, you're someone's precious boy, too...

967
48:17.397 --> 48:19.347
There.

968
48:25.405 --> 48:28.306
My, look at this.

969
48:28.306 --> 48:30.206
I should wash it.

970
48:53.584 --> 48:55.587
Oh my.

971
48:59.625 --> 49:01.826
Looks good.

972
49:01.826 --> 49:05.730
Dry already, will you?

973
49:06.905 --> 49:08.557
There you go.

974
49:08.557 --> 49:10.344
Looks good.

975
49:13.335 --> 49:16.997
[Oh Seok Jin]

976
49:31.463 --> 49:33.994
I'm so sorry, ma'am.

977
49:35.904 --> 49:37.286
The wall is collapsing...

978
49:37.286 --> 49:38.287
Look at that prick.

979
49:38.287 --> 49:39.370
You dummy!

980
49:39.370 --> 49:42.094
What are you doing in there? Get yourself out already!

981
49:52.462 --> 49:54.827
How did it get this late already?

982
49:54.827 --> 49:58.172
Seok Jin, we couldn't reach you, so we're heading back first.

983
49:58.172 --> 50:01.625
Take your time helping the old lady, then come back.

984
50:03.172 --> 50:05.719
Oh, ma'am...

985
50:06.390 --> 50:08.730
Thank you.

986
50:08.730 --> 50:10.562
Oh, it's cold.

987
50:10.562 --> 50:12.799
They aren't dry yet.

988
50:21.402 --> 50:22.952
What was that?

989
50:22.952 --> 50:25.255
I thought the lady wasn't here.

990
50:54.408 --> 50:56.110
Who are you?

991
51:03.255 --> 51:05.978
G-G-Ghost!

992
51:13.851 --> 51:15.059
Mom! Mom?

993
51:15.059 --> 51:17.664
He passed out!

994
51:29.089 --> 51:33.728
My, this soldier passes out at the drop of a hat.

995
51:34.898 --> 51:36.171
The dead son from the picture...

996
51:36.171 --> 51:37.855
What?

997
51:37.855 --> 51:41.655
What on earth did you tell him that he thinks I'm dead?

998
51:41.655 --> 51:43.797
You said he was somewhere in the sky...

999
51:43.797 --> 51:46.634
I did. He was in the sky.

1000
51:46.634 --> 51:51.378
My son is a pilot. A captain.

1001
51:55.018 --> 51:57.322
Did you say you came from the US today?

1002
51:57.322 --> 52:00.162
- Yes, and I came straight here. - Yes.

1003
52:00.162 --> 52:02.581
I can't come here very often.

1004
52:02.581 --> 52:04.512
So she gets lonely.

1005
52:04.512 --> 52:06.438
Whenever she sees a man in uniform,

1006
52:06.438 --> 52:09.638
she thinks of me and goes out of her way to take care of them.

1007
52:09.638 --> 52:12.479
Thanks to this young soldier today,

1008
52:12.479 --> 52:14.910
I got my house all fixed up.

1009
52:14.910 --> 52:20.379
It was so nice having someone around in my house again after so long.

1010
52:20.379 --> 52:21.380
Was it?

1011
52:21.380 --> 52:22.896
Yes.

1012
52:22.896 --> 52:24.714
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin?

1013
52:24.714 --> 52:26.450
Yes.

1014
52:26.450 --> 52:28.232
Thank you.

1015
52:28.232 --> 52:33.772
Seeing my mother smile like that again is such a relief.

1016
52:34.751 --> 52:40.697
Then I feel relieved, too. I feel like I've done my part.

1017
52:40.697 --> 52:43.244
Yes.

1018
52:44.659 --> 52:45.926
Take this.

1019
52:45.926 --> 52:48.216
It's mugwort rice cakes.

1020
52:48.216 --> 52:51.094
Take it to the camp and share it with other soldiers.

1021
52:51.094 --> 52:55.760
Even with my bad back, I went out and picked mugwort to make these rice cakes.

1022
52:55.760 --> 52:56.841
They should be good.

1023
52:56.841 --> 52:58.950
How could I accept something this precious...

1024
52:58.950 --> 53:01.812
Thank you. I'll enjoy this.

1025
53:01.812 --> 53:04.206
I'm sorry, you know, for everything.

1026
53:04.206 --> 53:07.348
I just know today was hard for you. I made you work so hard.

1027
53:07.348 --> 53:09.378
I'm sorry.

1028
53:10.249 --> 53:13.059
My son, you see, he's busy all the time.

1029
53:13.059 --> 53:14.608
Even on these rare occasions when he comes by to visit,

1030
53:14.608 --> 53:17.432
there's never enough time to get a good look at his face.

1031
53:17.432 --> 53:19.018
But anyway...

1032
53:19.018 --> 53:21.407
Mr. Soldier...

1033
53:21.407 --> 53:24.406
I actually had a great time just bickering with you all day.

1034
53:24.406 --> 53:27.021
It was so much fun!

1035
53:27.021 --> 53:28.295
Oh, thank you.

1036
53:28.295 --> 53:29.753
Treat him well, okay?

1037
53:29.753 --> 53:31.492
- Yes, Mother. - Good.

1038
53:31.492 --> 53:32.514
- Ma'am. - Yes?

1039
53:32.514 --> 53:33.668
I have to admit...

1040
53:33.668 --> 53:36.351
I had a lot of fun today, too.

1041
53:38.612 --> 53:39.970
Chungseong!

1042
53:39.970 --> 53:41.615
Oh, yeah, right.

1043
53:41.615 --> 53:43.044
First Lieutenant Oh Seok Jin!

1044
53:43.044 --> 53:46.738
Reporting in after a very successful civilian support mission!

1045
53:46.738 --> 53:48.019
Chungseong!

1046
53:48.019 --> 53:49.604
- Love you! - Alright.

1047
53:49.604 --> 53:50.697
- Ma'am! - Yes?

1048
53:50.697 --> 53:52.505
I wish you good health.

1049
53:53.156 --> 53:54.391
Okay, okay.

1050
53:54.391 --> 53:55.800
You did a good job today.

1051
53:55.800 --> 53:59.013
- Mr. Soldier. - Oh, it's nothing.

1052
53:59.013 --> 54:00.075
Go on, go.

1053
54:00.075 --> 54:01.726
- Alright, ma'am. I'll be going now. - Yes.

1054
54:01.726 --> 54:03.688
Goodbye.

1055
54:07.250 --> 54:08.297
Hey.

1056
54:08.297 --> 54:11.248
Come by anytime you're craving some noodles!

1057
54:11.248 --> 54:12.259
Yes, ma'am!

1058
54:12.259 --> 54:13.736
Bye!

1059
54:24.699 --> 54:26.239
Oh, one second, please.

1060
54:26.239 --> 54:27.693
What is it?

1061
54:33.451 --> 54:35.814
- Ma'am! - What? Why? What is it?

1062
54:35.814 --> 54:38.312
- What's the matter? - I...

1063
54:38.312 --> 54:39.655
I need to use the toilet.

1064
54:39.655 --> 54:41.195
What?

1065
54:41.940 --> 54:43.455
Over there.

1066
54:43.455 --> 54:44.859
- It's right over there. - Oh, okay.

1067
54:44.859 --> 54:48.208
Thank you, ma'am. That was a lot of noodles, if you get me.

1068
54:51.946 --> 54:54.967
Oh, you rotten bastard.

1069
54:56.075 --> 54:57.531
Communication security, Corporal No Hee Jeong speaking.

1070
54:57.531 --> 54:59.297
- Well, that's... - Oh, he hasn't come back yet.

1071
54:59.297 --> 55:01.929
- We'll report back as soon as he does. - As soon as he's back.

1072
55:01.929 --> 55:04.218
Yes, chungseong, sir!

1073
55:04.218 --> 55:06.407
Communication security, Corporal No Hee Jeong speaking.

1074
55:06.407 --> 55:08.454
Oh, we haven't been able to confirm that yet.

1075
55:08.454 --> 55:09.842
Communication security, this is the Second Company admin office.

1076
55:09.842 --> 55:12.092
- What can I help you with? - I have no idea, sir.

1077
55:12.092 --> 55:13.093
We're not sure yet...

1078
55:13.093 --> 55:14.815
Are you a journalist?

1079
55:14.815 --> 55:16.291
I'm not sure.

1080
55:16.291 --> 55:17.383
What? My name?

1081
55:17.383 --> 55:19.093
Hey, idiot! Why are you speaking to a journalist?

1082
55:19.093 --> 55:20.401
Hang up on him. Come on!

1083
55:20.401 --> 55:22.866
Y-yes, sir, I'll call you back right away...

1084
55:25.620 --> 55:27.628
Explain what's going on.

1085
55:30.499 --> 55:32.204
Communication security, this is the Second Company admin office.

1086
55:32.204 --> 55:33.959
What can I help you with...

1087
55:34.650 --> 55:35.651
First Sergeant...

1088
55:35.651 --> 55:38.867
It's that reporter again, from just now...

1089
55:48.683 --> 55:50.321
Mom! It's me!

1090
55:50.321 --> 55:51.934
I'm fine!

1091
55:51.934 --> 55:53.032
Yeah?

1092
55:53.032 --> 55:54.668
What shooting accident?

1093
55:54.668 --> 55:56.000
What are you even talking about?

1094
55:56.000 --> 55:58.233
There was no accident.

1095
55:58.233 --> 56:00.535
Nothing happened. Don't worry.

1096
56:00.535 --> 56:02.515
Yeah. Alright.

1097
56:03.907 --> 56:06.408
A shooting? No way.

1098
56:08.607 --> 56:10.557
Chungseong! Love you!

1099
56:11.281 --> 56:13.231
One moment, coming through!

1100
56:14.988 --> 56:16.045
Chungseong! Love you!

1101
56:16.045 --> 56:19.473
- Good work. - Great work, everyone.

1102
56:19.473 --> 56:21.673
- Did something happen? - What the heck, that scared me.

1103
56:21.673 --> 56:23.180
What's he going to do now?

1104
56:23.180 --> 56:24.460
He was supervising, right?

1105
56:24.460 --> 56:27.071
Wow. He's totally screwed.

1106
56:28.138 --> 56:30.185
What was that?

1107
56:31.883 --> 56:33.006
Hey, Yoon Mo.

1108
56:33.006 --> 56:34.612
Corporal Sung Yoon Mo!

1109
56:34.612 --> 56:37.312
What's going on? Did something happen?

1110
56:37.312 --> 56:39.262
Well... It's...

1111
56:41.067 --> 56:42.575
Corporal Park Min Seok...

1112
56:42.575 --> 56:43.724
Huh?

1113
56:43.724 --> 56:44.837
It's...

1114
56:44.837 --> 56:48.048
Someone posted something on the forum...

1115
56:48.048 --> 56:50.874
- Forum? - Yes, sir, that's right.

1116
56:53.633 --> 56:54.705
Great job, sir!

1117
56:54.705 --> 56:57.129
- You too. - Thank you, sir!

1118
56:57.832 --> 57:00.030
What did you do all day?

1119
57:00.030 --> 57:03.534
I was with Private First Class Jeon Se Gye, and cleaned the quarters, sir!

1120
57:03.534 --> 57:05.362
Did you hear anything unusual?

1121
57:05.362 --> 57:07.808
Well, what do you mean, sir?

1122
57:10.639 --> 57:12.057
Sergeant Kim Sang Hun.

1123
57:12.057 --> 57:14.848
I need to go speak with Hyeon Uk in private, outside.

1124
57:14.848 --> 57:16.526
Okay. Go ahead.

1125
57:16.526 --> 57:18.476
Thank you, sir.

1126
57:21.254 --> 57:22.856
Private Kim Hyeon Uk!

1127
57:22.856 --> 57:24.550
I'll be right back, sir.

1128
57:29.602 --> 57:31.654
Think it'll be alright, sir?

1129
57:31.654 --> 57:33.618
It's no surprise that Min Seok would assume so.

1130
57:33.618 --> 57:36.023
I knew this would happen ever since they made that forum.

1131
57:36.023 --> 57:37.896
Security is key in the army, right?

1132
57:37.896 --> 57:40.569
So how would a forum be a good idea in the first place?

1133
57:41.180 --> 57:43.275
Keep an eye on those two.

1134
57:43.275 --> 57:45.608
- Yes, sir. - Yes, sir.

1135
57:59.919 --> 58:01.474
Hyeon Uk.

1136
58:01.474 --> 58:03.286
Just use your words and say it to my face.

1137
58:03.286 --> 58:05.324
Don't go doing this behind my back.

1138
58:05.324 --> 58:07.768
I don't know what you mean.

1139
58:07.768 --> 58:09.294
I know it's you.

1140
58:09.294 --> 58:10.580
You wrote that post, didn't you?

1141
58:10.580 --> 58:12.674
About the blank shooting accident.

1142
58:12.674 --> 58:14.858
You really want to dig it back up and screw me over?

1143
58:14.858 --> 58:16.560
Is that why you did this?

1144
58:17.480 --> 58:20.891
You were the only one who stayed behind today. Who else can it possibly be?

1145
58:24.974 --> 58:26.587
Did you just sigh at me?

1146
58:26.587 --> 58:28.845
Sir, today...

1147
58:28.845 --> 58:31.660
I was with Private First Class Jeon Se Gye the entire day.

1148
58:31.660 --> 58:33.227
You...

1149
58:33.227 --> 58:34.478
If it isn't you...

1150
58:34.478 --> 58:35.985
If it's not...

1151
58:35.985 --> 58:39.495
- I'm going to, I swear I'll... - What are you going to do, then?

1152
58:39.495 --> 58:41.705
You'll just kick me out again, huh?

1153
58:42.429 --> 58:43.487
What?

1154
58:43.487 --> 58:45.284
It's nothing, sir.

1155
58:46.292 --> 58:48.150
Whatever I do...

1156
58:48.150 --> 58:49.727
It doesn't even matter.

1157
58:49.727 --> 58:52.001
I'm the one who loses every time.

1158
58:53.767 --> 58:56.205
"Every time?"

1159
58:56.205 --> 58:57.551
Corporal Park Min Seok.

1160
58:57.551 --> 58:59.366
I'm just going to head inside.

1161
59:00.536 --> 59:02.876
What do you mean by "lose?"

1162
59:08.235 --> 59:09.885
What do you...

1163
59:14.628 --> 59:17.864
The reason why I couldn't tell you what was going on right away...

1164
59:17.864 --> 59:19.645
was because of the other soldiers there.

1165
59:19.645 --> 59:22.181
I didn't want to cause a scene.

1166
59:22.181 --> 59:25.031
- I hope you understand. - Of course, sir.

1167
59:25.668 --> 59:29.129
I took the post down as soon as I got back,

1168
59:29.129 --> 59:32.905
but it seems it has already made its way around through various forums.

1169
59:32.905 --> 59:35.468
[Report on malicious posts regarding the camp]

1170
59:35.468 --> 59:38.869
I managed to keep the news from being spread through some journalists I know, but...

1171
59:38.869 --> 59:40.594
The problem is...

1172
59:40.594 --> 59:42.622
The higher-ups have noticed that something is wrong.

1173
59:42.622 --> 59:45.154
[It's serious if it's real] And I checked the IP address, too.

1174
59:45.154 --> 59:46.428
The post was made on the camp grounds.

1175
59:46.428 --> 59:47.429
[Is this the truth about Shinhwa Unit?]

1176
59:47.429 --> 59:49.233
[They covered up a shooting accident...] Request the military investigation agency

1177
59:49.233 --> 59:50.889
[for a battalion commander's promotion.] for a history log

1178
59:50.889 --> 59:54.373
of this post through the camp network.

1179
59:54.373 --> 59:56.655
Let's get this guy, quick.

1180
01:00:00.108 --> 01:00:01.715
Got something to say?

1181
01:00:01.715 --> 01:00:03.509
No, sir...

1182
01:00:03.509 --> 01:00:04.928
But if I may,

1183
01:00:04.928 --> 01:00:07.014
I would like to share my opinion, sir.

1184
01:00:07.014 --> 01:00:09.325
Sure, go on ahead.

1185
01:00:09.325 --> 01:00:11.816
Well, I've been thinking...

1186
01:00:11.816 --> 01:00:14.901
But I'm not sure if the poster is in the wrong,

1187
01:00:14.901 --> 01:00:16.115
or...

1188
01:00:16.115 --> 01:00:19.312
If the person responsible for the issue being discussed is the wrong one.

1189
01:00:19.312 --> 01:00:20.823
I haven't made up my mind,

1190
01:00:20.823 --> 01:00:23.563
so I haven't been able to request an investigation yet, sir.

1191
01:00:26.278 --> 01:00:27.946
So what you're saying is,

1192
01:00:27.946 --> 01:00:31.253
the source of the problem must be the commander who made a forum in the first place?

1193
01:00:31.253 --> 01:00:33.477
Is that correct?

1194
01:00:41.569 --> 01:00:43.420
Second Company Commander.

1195
01:00:43.420 --> 01:00:45.402
Do you remember what I told you before?

1196
01:00:45.402 --> 01:00:46.561
Yes, sir.

1197
01:00:46.561 --> 01:00:50.083
If we punish a soldier, it's a sign that our unit has fallen behind.

1198
01:00:50.083 --> 01:00:52.329
The higher-ups should take responsibility.

1199
01:00:52.329 --> 01:00:54.631
The commanders should take responsibility.

1200
01:00:55.355 --> 01:00:56.978
So...

1201
01:00:56.978 --> 01:00:59.128
I'm going to take responsibility.

1202
01:01:04.234 --> 01:01:06.281
It was my order.

1203
01:01:06.281 --> 01:01:07.754
Yet you want to be held responsible for it?

1204
01:01:07.754 --> 01:01:10.072
It happened in the Second Company.

1205
01:01:10.072 --> 01:01:12.028
Moreover...

1206
01:01:12.028 --> 01:01:14.586
I am the commander of the Second Company.

1207
01:01:15.617 --> 01:01:17.929
We're in the middle of a promotion evaluation.

1208
01:01:17.929 --> 01:01:19.879
Are you sure about this?

1209
01:01:20.522 --> 01:01:22.972
Yes, sir. I'm sure.

1210
01:01:38.541 --> 01:01:42.073
[Company Commander, Captain Cho Baek Ho]

1211
01:01:51.879 --> 01:01:55.080
[Shinhwa Second Company Order of Battle]

1212
01:01:57.268 --> 01:01:58.829
Come in.

1213
01:02:01.328 --> 01:02:03.195
First Sergeant! What are you doing here at this hour?

1214
01:02:03.195 --> 01:02:05.553
Oh, I figured you might be having a rough time.

1215
01:02:05.553 --> 01:02:08.137
So I decided to drop by in case you haven't gone home yet.

1216
01:02:08.137 --> 01:02:10.128
Don't tell me you're empty-handed.

1217
01:02:10.793 --> 01:02:12.001
No way.

1218
01:02:12.001 --> 01:02:13.460
Ta-da.

1219
01:02:14.373 --> 01:02:16.044
Come with me.

1220
01:02:17.414 --> 01:02:19.452
It looks so good!

1221
01:02:19.452 --> 01:02:21.508
- Go on, dig in. - Yes.

1222
01:02:21.508 --> 01:02:26.227
Oh, right. I heard that the battalion commander rushed to the division headquarters earlier.

1223
01:02:26.227 --> 01:02:29.048
Well, that was fast.

1224
01:02:29.048 --> 01:02:31.778
Did something happen between the two of you?

1225
01:02:31.778 --> 01:02:34.161
Nothing big, really.

1226
01:02:34.161 --> 01:02:36.367
I just had a talk with him.

1227
01:02:37.010 --> 01:02:39.229
I told him I'd take full responsibility.

1228
01:02:39.229 --> 01:02:40.919
What?

1229
01:02:40.919 --> 01:02:44.438
Oh, no, there's no need for you to do that.

1230
01:02:44.438 --> 01:02:47.332
It'll all blow over soon if you just keep quiet and wait.

1231
01:02:47.332 --> 01:02:48.974
I'm just not made for it, I guess.

1232
01:02:48.974 --> 01:02:51.836
Keeping quiet, waiting for something to pass...

1233
01:02:52.530 --> 01:02:55.012
It's promotion evaluation season, though...

1234
01:02:55.012 --> 01:02:58.231
This is just how it's destined to be. I've come to terms with it.

1235
01:02:58.231 --> 01:03:01.659
That is some cruel destiny, no doubt about it.

1236
01:03:01.659 --> 01:03:03.688
You can say that again, sir.

1237
01:03:03.688 --> 01:03:06.753
Seems I'll be decommissioned sooner than I anticipated!

1238
01:03:08.250 --> 01:03:10.133
I want to laugh with you, I do,

1239
01:03:10.133 --> 01:03:12.270
but I can't bring myself to.

1240
01:03:12.934 --> 01:03:14.542
I just know you haven't eaten anything today.

1241
01:03:14.542 --> 01:03:15.657
Go on, eat up.

1242
01:03:15.657 --> 01:03:17.321
Yes, sir. Thank you.

1243
01:03:17.321 --> 01:03:19.546
I'd never let your kindness go to waste, sir.

1244
01:03:22.921 --> 01:03:25.061
This tteokbokki is so good.

1245
01:03:25.061 --> 01:03:28.958
Tteokbokki tastes best when you get it for me, sir.

1246
01:03:30.368 --> 01:03:32.055
From now on...

1247
01:03:35.388 --> 01:03:37.985
T-Try some of those fried sides, too.

1248
01:03:37.985 --> 01:03:40.747
It's fresh out of the fryer. I'm sure it's delicious.

1249
01:03:42.708 --> 01:03:44.341
All this time...

1250
01:03:44.341 --> 01:03:46.552
Thank you for everything, First Sergeant.

1251
01:03:46.552 --> 01:03:47.801
Really,

1252
01:03:47.801 --> 01:03:49.911
if it weren't for you...

1253
01:03:49.911 --> 01:03:51.054
I would've...

1254
01:03:51.054 --> 01:03:53.559
Oh, stop! Get back to eating your tteokbokki.

1255
01:03:53.559 --> 01:03:55.809
Go on, eat, eat!

1256
01:03:56.561 --> 01:03:58.142
No, sir. What I meant was,

1257
01:03:58.142 --> 01:04:01.401
I would've missed out on this amazing tteokbokki if it weren't for you!

1258
01:04:01.401 --> 01:04:04.128
Oh, you silly goose.

1259
01:04:04.128 --> 01:04:06.124
Wow, it's just so good.

1260
01:04:06.721 --> 01:04:08.951
I really appreciate this, sir.

1261
01:04:24.888 --> 01:04:26.314
It doesn't even matter.

1262
01:04:26.314 --> 01:04:28.555
I'm the one who loses every time.

1263
01:04:37.741 --> 01:04:39.516
Chungseong, love you.

1264
01:04:39.516 --> 01:04:41.412
Oh, hi, Se Gye.

1265
01:04:41.412 --> 01:04:42.828
Can't sleep, sir?

1266
01:04:42.828 --> 01:04:44.723
Yeah, I couldn't fall asleep.

1267
01:04:44.723 --> 01:04:46.581
You did a good job today.

1268
01:04:46.581 --> 01:04:47.581
Thank you.

1269
01:04:47.581 --> 01:04:48.922
Enjoy your ramen.

1270
01:04:48.922 --> 01:04:50.716
Yes, sir. Thank you.

1271
01:04:52.549 --> 01:04:54.134
Sir?

1272
01:04:56.232 --> 01:04:57.628
Corporal Park Min Seok.

1273
01:04:57.628 --> 01:04:59.017
Yes?

1274
01:05:00.271 --> 01:05:01.960
I have something I need to tell you, sir.

1275
01:05:01.960 --> 01:05:02.961
What is it?

1276
01:05:02.961 --> 01:05:04.911
Excuse me.

1277
01:05:19.421 --> 01:05:21.749
Are you sure about that?

1278
01:05:21.749 --> 01:05:23.381
Yes, sir.

1279
01:05:36.501 --> 01:05:37.570
Hey, it's me.

1280
01:05:37.570 --> 01:05:39.747
Want to hear something funny as hell?

1281
01:05:39.747 --> 01:05:41.781
We've got Park Min Seok here.

1282
01:05:41.781 --> 01:05:44.412
Yeah, that idiot, you remember?

1283
01:05:45.879 --> 01:05:48.280
Oh, dear Min Seok...

1284
01:05:48.280 --> 01:05:50.058
What's going on now?

1285
01:05:50.058 --> 01:05:51.691
About Hyeon Uk, sir...

1286
01:05:51.691 --> 01:05:53.245
Is he okay?

1287
01:05:53.245 --> 01:05:54.693
It's only natural if you're nervous.

1288
01:05:54.693 --> 01:05:56.748
I did the same thing as a private.

1289
01:05:56.748 --> 01:05:58.698
He's new here.

1290
01:05:59.955 --> 01:06:00.969
How did that get there?

1291
01:06:00.969 --> 01:06:04.602
I was with Private First Class Jeon Se Gye the entire day.

1292
01:06:05.969 --> 01:06:07.303
- You're back, sir! - Yeah.

1293
01:06:07.303 --> 01:06:09.540
May I use the restroom, sir?

1294
01:06:14.452 --> 01:06:16.106
It's hot...

1295
01:06:41.638 --> 01:06:43.119
Hey, you.

1296
01:06:44.062 --> 01:06:45.648
What's your problem?

1297
01:06:45.648 --> 01:06:48.121
Why are you doing this to me? Why?

1298
01:06:48.729 --> 01:06:50.980
What are you doing, sir?

1299
01:06:52.088 --> 01:06:54.039
You little piece of...

1300
01:06:57.008 --> 01:06:58.958
See me outside. Quietly.

1301
01:07:03.621 --> 01:07:06.380
Why can't we just talk here?

1302
01:07:06.380 --> 01:07:08.219
What?

1303
01:07:08.219 --> 01:07:10.284
Well, Corporal Park Min Seok...

1304
01:07:10.284 --> 01:07:12.725
You can do whatever you want in here, no?

1305
01:07:15.711 --> 01:07:17.761
You bastard!
